The usual apologies in case everyone and his grandmother knows
this already.  Spoiler ahead (I prefer to think of them as
technology transfer):

Next time you're trying to figure out what to do with that cursed
scroll of genocide you've been lugging around, try this.  Read it
and select as your victims the fearsome kraken.  Bam, there you
are surrounded by the hideous beasts, and they're mad!  But there's
just one minor problem: no water.  Kraken, being sea monsters, don't
do real well on dry land.  They just sort of flop around hoping to
find water.  Although they aren't peaceful, they don't attack.  And
they lose a hit point each turn; after about a hundred turns, they're
down to one (they apparently never die from being out of water).
This is where you come in.  Saunter up to one of these monstrousities,
poke it with your pathetic little weapon, and it dies -- and you get
over a thousand experience points.  Eat corpse, get very fat.  Repeat
as needed on the remaining kraken.  I'd imagine a kraken corpse would
make a fine sacrifice, especially if your god likes seafood.

Since the kraken don't fight with you, it doesn't matter how wimpy your
person, armor, or weapons are.  However, I've noticed that they will
strike back when cornered, so only hit them when it is possible for
them to move away from you.

This also works with the other sea monsters, the giant eel and the
electric eel.  You might want to try it with the electric eel, as
eating their corpses can confer shock resistance, and this is an E-Z
way to get a bunch of them.

